  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Enter a redshift and a cosmology (preset or custom H0, Ωm, ΩΛ, Ωr, w0, wa) to get the comoving, transverse comoving, luminosity and angular-diameter distances, comoving volume, lookback time and the physical size of 1 arcsec at that redshift; plot these from z=0 to that redshift; and download the plots as PDF and the data table as a text file. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
